.TH TULPAR-GRAPH 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.2.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-graph \- export the installed package dependency graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar graph
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar p
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-p
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds libapg's dependency graph from every installed package and
exports it in Graphviz DOT format. Every package is a node (installed
ones filled green), every dependency is an edge to whatever provider
libapg would currently resolve it to (labeled with the version
constraint, if any; drawn red and dashed if unresolved), and every
virtual
.RI ( provides )
name is a diamond node with an edge to each of its providers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Inspect the package database of an alternate root instead of the live
system.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Write the DOT source to
.I path
instead of standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the database cannot be opened or the graph
cannot be exported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1),
.BR tulpar-verify (1)
